# Server Data Flow

Reads happen in Server Components. Inserts/updates/deletes happen in Server Actions. Server Action inputs are typed and validated with Zod — never `FormData`. All database reads and writes go through helper functions in `src/db/queries` — never call `db` / Drizzle directly from pages, layouts, or Server Actions.

- Fetch data in an `async` Server Component (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, or server-only child) by calling a query helper from `@/db/queries`. Pass resolved data as props to Client Components.
- Never fetch initial data from the client (`useEffect` + `fetch`, SWR/React Query against your own API) when a Server Component could load it.
- Every insert/update/delete is a `"use server"` function that calls a mutation helper from `@/db/queries`. Never call `db.insert` / `db.update` / `db.delete` (or any other Drizzle API) from a Client Component, Server Component, Server Action, or client-triggered `fetch`.
- Put Drizzle access only in `src/db/queries` (e.g. `src/db/queries/decks.ts`, `src/db/queries/cards.ts`). Group helpers by domain; export typed functions that accept `userId` (and other IDs) and return only the fields callers need.
- Server Action parameters use an explicit TypeScript type (`z.infer<typeof schema>`). Do not type a parameter as `FormData` — build the typed object on the caller side and pass that in.
- Validate every Server Action input with Zod (`parse`/`safeParse`) before calling a query helper. Zod checks shape only — it does not replace ownership checks.
- Route Handlers are not for app CRUD — reserve `route.ts` for webhooks, external API consumers, or GETs the app itself must `fetch()`. Client-triggered DB writes use Server Actions.
- Every Server Action still calls `auth()` and passes `userId` into the query helper, which scopes the query/mutation by ownership (see clerk-data-isolation).
- After a mutation, call `revalidatePath`/`revalidateTag` (or `redirect`) so the owning Server Component re-fetches. Don't hand-patch client state.

```ts
// src/db/queries/decks.ts
import { eq } from "drizzle-orm";
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decks } from "@/db/schema";

export async function createDeckForUser(userId: string, title: string) {
  await db.insert(decks).values({ userId, title });
}

export async function listDecksForUser(userId: string) {
  return db
    .select({ id: decks.id, title: decks.title })
    .from(decks)
    .where(eq(decks.userId, userId));
}
```

```ts
// Server Action
"use server";
const createDeckSchema = z.object({ title: z.string().trim().min(1).max(120) });
type CreateDeckInput = z.infer<typeof createDeckSchema>;

export async function createDeck(input: CreateDeckInput) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");
  const { title } = createDeckSchema.parse(input);
  await createDeckForUser(userId, title);
  revalidatePath("/decks");
}
```
